%I A401319 #11 Oct 29 2026 23:31:19
%S A401319 1,1,3,11,42,161,618,2372,9105,34949,134151,514934,1976559,7586960,
%T A401319 29122314,111785105,429083691,1647024551,6322053102,24267006437,
%U A401319 93148158066,357546340640,1372430634873,5268032792981,20221181896515,77618384956850,297935784077667
%N A401319 Number of fixed point free involutions in S_{2n} (or perfect matchings on [2n]) which avoid the patterns {123, 132, 213, 321}.
%C A401319 a(n) is the number of perfect matchings on [2n] that simultaneously avoid the patterns 123, 132, 213, and 321, where pattern avoidance for matchings is in the sense of Bloom and Elizalde. The term a(0)=1 corresponds to the empty matching.
%H A401319 Sucharita Biswas, Umesh Shankar, and Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.01996">Matchings and shape-Wilf-Equivalence of sets of patterns of length three II: Quadruples and Quintuples</a>, arXiv:2610.01996 [math.CO], 2026. See Theorem 30.
%H A401319 Jonathan Bloom and Sergi Elizalde, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/2976">Pattern avoidance in matchings and partitions</a>, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 20(2) (2013), #P5.
%H A401319 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,4,-3).
%F A401319 G.f.: (1 - 2*x - 4*x^2 + x^3)/(1 - 3*x - 4*x^2 + 3*x^3).
%F A401319 a(0)=1, a(1)=1, a(2)=3, a(3)=11, and for n >= 4, a(n) = 3*a(n-1) + 4*a(n-2) - 3*a(n-3).
%e A401319 a(4)=42 is the number of perfect matchings on [8] avoiding the patterns 123, 132, 213, and 321.
%e A401319 a(5)=161 is the number of perfect matchings on [10] avoiding these four patterns.
%Y A401319 Cf. A400996 (perfect matchings avoiding 123, 231, and 321).
%K A401319 nonn,easy,new
%O A401319 0,3
%A A401319 _Sucharita Biswas_, Oct 20 2026
